{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A2",
  "unit": 4,
  "title": "The day",
  "description": "Say when it is, and when things happen.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Telling the time in Spanish has one irregularity that catches everybody: after la una you do not say las, and after every other hour you do.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "La una and las demás",
        "body": "Es la una is one o'clock. Everything else is es las: es las dos, es las cinco, es las once. After la una you say la una y media, but after any other hour you say las tres y media. The same rule applies to the quarter: las cuatro y cuarto, but la una y cuarto.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Es la una.",
            "en": "It is one o'clock."
          },
          {
            "es": "Son las tres y media.",
            "en": "It is half past three."
          },
          {
            "es": "Son las diez menos veinte.",
            "en": "It is twenty to ten."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "A time of day is feminine",
        "body": "La mañana, la tarde and la noche are all feminine, so you say por la mañana, por la tarde, por la noche. A day of the week is masculine instead, which is the opposite of English: el lunes, el martes. Do not mix them up.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Trabajo por la mañana.",
            "en": "I work in the morning."
          },
          {
            "es": "El lunes tengo una reunión.",
            "en": "On Monday I have a meeting."
          },
          {
            "es": "Estudio por la tarde.",
            "en": "I study in the afternoon."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Saying when something happens",
        "body": "A specific time goes with a, not con: a las tres, a las nueve de la noche. To say something happens every day, use todos los días or cada día. And for a time range, de a: de nueve a cinco.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "La reunión es a las tres.",
            "en": "The meeting is at three."
          },
          {
            "es": "Trabajo de nueve a cinco.",
            "en": "I work from nine to five."
          },
          {
            "es": "Estudio todos los días.",
            "en": "I study every day."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
